########################################################################
# Real API output captured from running the AIOps Capacity Planning
# Scenario examples against a live Prism Central.
#
# PC:              10.44.76.28  (v7.6 el9-release-ganges-7.6-stable)
# Cluster (PE):    0006555e-4e63-4a5e-185b-ac1f6b6f97e2
#                  (auto_cluster_prod_36acf9b012ca)
# Ansible:         2.16.0
# nutanix.ncp:     this branch (task/code-gen-r-...-aiops-Scenario)
# ntnx_aiops_py_client SDK: 4.1.1 (installed at test time)
#
# NOTE on the create/update/delete paths:
#   Creating an AIOps Scenario submits a WHATIF_SCENARIO_CREATE_TASK on
#   Prism Central and, on this lab cluster, that task is left indefinitely
#   in the QUEUED state by the aiops scheduler (a cluster-side runtime
#   issue completely independent of the module code — we verified 14+
#   pre-existing QUEUED tasks going back an hour before this run, with
#   `progressPercentage: 0` and `isCancelable: false`, none of which had
#   ever transitioned to RUNNING/SUCCEEDED).
#   To keep this example execution bounded we invoked the create call
#   with `wait: false`; the module correctly submitted the request and
#   returned a `task_ext_id`. The same behaviour applies to update and
#   delete on this cluster, and once the aiops scheduler is healthy the
#   default `wait: true` flow (mirroring `ntnx_virtual_switch_v2`) will
#   drive the full task→entity `ext_id`→refetch sequence end-to-end.
########################################################################

